Id: decoded-nul-dropped
Title: A decoded NUL is dropped
Input: Text that is repaired by decoding bytes with the codec
 utf-8-variants, where the bytes hold C0 80, Java's encoding of U+0000.
 For example 'null\u00c0\u20acseparated', whose characters U+00C0
 U+20AC encode in sloppy-windows-1252 to C0 80. Also a plan replayed
 with apply_plan() whose step 'decode utf-8-variants' meets C0 80.
Reference: U+0000 in place of each C0 80. Run on ftfy 6.3.1 with Python
 3.13: b'null\xc0\x80separated'.decode('utf-8-variants') and
 fix_encoding('null\u00c0\u20acseparated') both return
 'null\x00separated'. fix_text() of the same text returns
 'nullseparated', because its fixer remove_control_chars then removes
 the U+0000.
R: Nothing in place of each C0 80, because an R string cannot hold
 U+0000: the decoder and fix_encoding() give 'nullseparated'. fix_text()
 with default options gives the same text as the reference version.
Decided: docs/adr/0007-a-decoded-nul-is-dropped.md
